<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Ba Vi by Motorbike: Luggage Packing Guide</h1>
<p>A motorbike carries its rider, its rider&rsquo;s safety and its rider&rsquo;s luggage, and only one of those three gets to be placed carelessly before the trip goes wrong. The Ba Vi day asks a small, honest amount of cargo, a rain layer, water, a warm top, documents and the small kit, and the difference between a good packing job and a bad one is not the list, it is the physics: where the weight sits, how it is protected and how it is attached to a machine that will spend the day moving through weather.</p>
<p>The bike, the rack and the cargo advice can all be arranged at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk straps western-trip luggage every day and answers the packing questions this guide raises. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, read the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/hanoi-to-ba-vi-motorbike-route/">Ba Vi route guide</a>, see the fleet and the terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The Physics Of Weight On Two Wheels</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The Day-Trip List, Kept Honest</a></li>
